# (build 132) A note sounding on through a pause (The owner, on 131c: "a lot of
# synth note sustain when I push pause", both synths). Shure under its music
# (Music_Advanced), VOICES EXTRA (the default): the tick before the pause
# takes hold, music slot 3's chord strikes a pad note across FM3-FM5, and
# the pause jingle has lent FM4 and FM5, so the one chip never hears the
# pad there -- but EXTRA's music chip does, and the pause's walk (as the
# ROM's) skips parts lent to an effect. The pad rang on at -35 dBFS 90
# ticks in. Now the pause keys off, on the hooks alone, every music part
# lent to an effect; the chip's own writes are unchanged. Fails on 131c,
# passes on 132. (Aukba and the dams measured -43 and -48 before, under the
# -40 this expects; silent too now: docs/history.md, Build 132.)

start slot 1 routes/saves/paseo_recorder.json
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait screen level
wait idle
warp 0x17 24 12
wait screen level
wait idle
sound render on
wait ticks 300
press start
wait ticks 90
expect sound silent          # the jingle's release gone, no pad
